-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a819d76b-22a0-404d-83e6-621366d20234
-- title:
--   Verified initialization of the retained color-layout header
-- statement:
--   Let $n,g>0$ and $f\in\mathbb N$. Put $b=\lceil n/g\rceil$, $R=3b^2$, $a=f+11+4n$, $t=f+17+13n$, and $e=t+(5+3g)R$. These determine the retained color-array layout. Let $S,W,D$ be machine limits, with $S\le W$, $e+1\le S$, $n+g+R+100\le W$, and starting depth $d<D$. Suppose $P$ contains the layout body and its small-division helper. From any integer memory $\mu$, execution on $(n,g,f)$ finishes within $20b+1020$ steps and satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   r&=e,\\
--   \nu[f:f+8]&=[a,a+n,a+3n+2,a+4n+2,\\
--   &\qquad a+6n+4,a+7n+4,t+R,t+5R].
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   All memory below $f$ is preserved. The eight entries are the three value/endpoint pairs followed by the record and raw-value bases.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightEncodedColorLayout.lean#L62-L137

